In article <759@lll-crg.ARPA> you write:
>
>	I have been playing for a few weeks and just can't figure out how to
>use some of the things I've found.  I'd appreciate some hints. . .
>
>	What can you use a blank scroll for?
Absolutely Nothing

>	Is there any way to find out whats in a tin without eating it?
No

>	What is a potion that causes 'Your legs feel better' msg to appear
>	called?  What does a xan do when it pricks your legs? You collapse
>	under your load, but your strength remains the same.  Any way to avoid
>	these little pricks (pun intended)?
A potion of speed will heal your legs.  Also, eating royal jelly will work too.
When a xan pricks your legs he injures them so you cannot carry all of your
goodies anymore.  You must either quaff a potion of speed, eat royal jelly,
or drop some stuff.  You can avoid these little pricks by reading a scroll
of genocide and trashing them.

>	I killed a dragon, but even dropping everything, and with 18/00
>	strength couldn't lift it.  I read in the notes that eating one had
>	a side effect, so how do I do it?
You don't need to pick something up to eat it.  Just move on top of it by
typing "m" followed by the direction.  To look at what is under you type ":"
Once you are over the dragon, type "e" and you will be prompted whether you
want to eat the dragon.  Munching mister dragon gives you fire resistance.

>	Is there a way to get beyond levels with mazes?
No.  Lowest level is 39 which is a maze.

>	I'd also like to hear of any other clever tricks people have thought
>	out or discovered such as reading scrolls when confused to make them
>	do novel things.
Reading a scroll of teleportation while confused will teleport you to
a different level.  There is more to this, but you will figure it out
if you think about it.

If you read an enchant armor or enchant weapon scroll while confused, you
will "rust-proof" the item it affects.  This is good protection from R's.

